drag is about empowerment we travel  across this country to take people from  who they are to what they can be  this project has always spoken directly  to my heart  because i grew up in a small  conservative town and being able to have  the opportunity to travel around america  and amplify voices in small conservative  towns queer voices tell the stories the  struggles the triumphs all of that is a  gift to me going into these small  conservative towns i must imagine for  you by the time you leave you just must  feel this incredible sense of wow we did  that we changed some people's  perceptions of the queer community and  the art form of drag i'll never forget  after evansville indiana  [Music]  sorry  he's had to exist in this world of fear  what made you want to do drag here i  don't want to hide no more i don't want  to conceal no more me and luscious my  makeup artist sat in the car and we just  cried  and we were just so happy for case from  the time that we had met him when we  first got there just seeing him blossom  and then seeing you know him come out  and embrace all of who he was you know  through his drag character and through  the stage performance and hearing that  audience like  in a place where he always felt isolated  you know  and afraid so many times to have the  courage to be on stage and to perform  and to feel that spirit of community  that he didn't know existed  [Applause]  and to see that  and know that we had a a part in that  was like  it was just beautiful
 

